      "episode_id": "VR-478287",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Juror-1 independent check of the MSKU7720914 weight declaration, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nSumming the twelve pallet weights as printed: 1,820 + 1,795 + 1,840 + 1,760 + 1,905 + 1,688 + 1,742 + 1,810 + 1,655 + 1,930 + 1,701 + 1,840 = 21,486 kg. Adding dunnage and lashing of 240 kg gives a declared cargo gross weight of 21,726 kg, excluding container tare as the record specifies.\n\n21,726 kg is under 24,000 kg, by a margin of 2,274 kg - about 9.5% of the threshold. The claim as worded is therefore supported, and the margin is wide enough that a small transcription error in any single pallet would not change the conclusion.\n\nOn the container tare of 3,750 kg: it is expressly excluded by both the declaration and the claim ('excluding tare'), so it does not enter the figure. I note that adding it would give 25,476 kg, which is over 24,000 - so the exclusion matters to the result and the claim should be read as it is written. Reading it as including tare would misstate what the record declares.\n\nFor completeness: the pallets alone come to 21,486 kg, also under the threshold, so the conclusion does not depend on the dunnage treatment either. The declared figure is 5,004 kg under the 26,730 kg maximum cargo payload for this container type, so there is no capacity inconsistency in the declaration.\n\nOn this record the claim is supported. I find no unsupported element and no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0xa003aeaa6b143395025f54567500c16649ef3241542524533bc601c4905a601e",
          "created_at_ms": 1793327248046,
          "message_id": "c78145d8-df2a-4f41-9bbf-85aa244b8b5c",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger's review of the weight declaration for container MSKU7720914 against the packing list:\n\nSumming the twelve pallet lines:\n  01 1,820; 02 1,795; 03 1,840; 04 1,760; 05 1,905; 06 1,688;\n  07 1,742; 08 1,810; 09 1,655; 10 1,930; 11 1,701; 12 1,840\n  Pallets subtotal = 21,486 kg\n  Plus dunnage and lashing = 240 kg\n  Declared cargo gross weight (pallets plus dunnage, excluding tare) = 21,726 kg\n\n21,726 kg is under 24,000 kg by 2,274 kg, so the claim as worded holds.\n\nOne point worth flagging, since it changes the answer if mishandled: the container tare of 3,750 kg must NOT be added. The claim is explicit that it is excluding tare, and the packing list defines the declared cargo gross weight as the sum of the pallet lines plus dunnage. Adding tare would give 25,476 kg, which is over 24,000, but that is the container's own weight rather than cargo and is not what the claim asserts. The declared figure is 21,726 kg.\n\nFor completeness the figure is also within the 26,730 kg maximum cargo payload for this container type, so there is no capacity issue either. The weights are from a calibrated floor scale under certificate WS-2026-0441.\n\nOn this evidence I am not challenging the claim.",
          "content_hash": "0xad1e92ac369f5531515419bee58539065f6b9a8894bfdb4a486763666175caa7",
          "created_at_ms": 1793327252636,
          "message_id": "2e0ce812-b8db-4774-964e-6fe01fcaa49d",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 independent check of the weight declaration for container MSKU7720914, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nSumming the twelve pallet lines exactly as printed: 1,820 + 1,795 + 1,840 + 1,760 + 1,905 + 1,688 + 1,742 + 1,810 + 1,655 + 1,930 + 1,701 + 1,840 = 21,486 kg. Adding dunnage and lashing of 240 kg gives a declared cargo gross weight of 21,486 + 240 = 21,726 kg.\n\n21,726 kg is under the 24,000 kg threshold by 2,274 kg, so the claim as worded holds. The margin is about 9.5% of the threshold, and the pallets alone (21,486 kg) are also under it, so the conclusion does not depend on the dunnage treatment.\n\nThe one adjustment that would flip the answer is the container tare of 3,750 kg. I checked it and did not apply it: the claim expressly excludes tare, and the packing list defines the declared cargo gross weight as the sum of the pallet lines plus dunnage. Adding tare would give 21,726 + 3,750 = 25,476 kg, which is over 24,000, but that is the container's own weight rather than cargo, and the claim is about cargo weight excluding tare. Reading the exclusion away would misstate what the record declares, so I read the claim as written.\n\nI also checked capacity for consistency: 21,726 kg is 5,004 kg below the 26,730 kg maximum cargo payload for this container type, and even the tare-inclusive 25,476 kg stays below that maximum, so the declaration is not internally inconsistent. Weights are from the shipper's calibrated floor scale under certificate WS-2026-0441.\n\nOn this record the claim is supported. I find no unsupported element and no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0x9a8a6b44a3e3af34edc9a4bc7ae56700b8c593db6714d71061ba6c7c6b3b8efd",
          "created_at_ms": 1793327271019,
          "message_id": "d68c5d98-b822-41ed-8d9f-95f61c176942",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 independent check of container MSKU7720914's weight declaration, from the case record alone (round 1).\n\nClaim tested: \"The declared cargo gross weight, including dunnage and excluding tare, is under 24,000 kg.\"\n\nSumming all twelve pallet lines: 1,820 + 1,795 + 1,840 + 1,760 + 1,905 + 1,688 + 1,742 + 1,810 + 1,655 + 1,930 + 1,701 + 1,840 = 21,486 kg. Pallet numbers 01 to 12 are all present, so no line is missing or duplicated.\n\nAdding the stated dunnage and lashing of 240 kg: 21,486 + 240 = 21,726 kg declared cargo gross weight, excluding container tare as the claim specifies.\n\n21,726 kg is under 24,000 kg, by a margin of 2,274 kg, so the claim holds.\n\nThe one reading that would defeat it is to add the container tare of 3,750 kg, giving 25,476 kg. But the claim expressly excludes tare, and the record defines declared cargo gross weight as pallets plus dunnage excluding tare, so that reading contradicts the claim's own terms and I do not adopt it. Even the pallets alone (21,486 kg) are under the threshold, so the claim does not depend on the dunnage treatment either. The declared figure is also within the 26,730 kg maximum payload for this container type.\n\nOn the record as filed the claim holds, and I note no uncertainty in the arithmetic.",
          "content_hash": "0xa62741b8a5eb3ae121555203f8cdd19573e7e9eeb61781bf90cbaeef018e2af1",
          "created_at_ms": 1793327294776,
          "message_id": "19f61c80-3c61-4fee-8048-23eaf4dfda9d",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 4
        }
      ],
